// EXECUTION HIERARCHY (MANDATORY ORDER):
// 1. ICT Kill Zone Check (Time Filter)
// 2. Market Structure Detection (Bias)
// 3. Liquidity Sweep Detection (Entry Trigger)
// 4. Displacement Confirmation
// 5. Premium/Discount Zone Check
// 6. FVG/OB Mitigation (Entry Location)
// 7. Indicator Confirmation (Secondary)
// 8. Risk Filters
// 9. Execute Trade
//
// CRITICAL RULES:
// - Liquidity sweep MUST occur before trade
// - Structure determines bias only
// - Indicators CANNOT override context
// - One trade per liquidity event
// - SL beyond liquidity extreme
// - TP at opposing liquidity
//
// TESTING RECOMMENDATIONS:
// 1. Test on DEMO first
// 2. Verify structure detection manually
// 3. Check liquidity pool identification
// 4. Confirm kill zone times match your broker GMT offset
// 5. Monitor spread during your sessions
// 6. Start with 0.5% risk
//
// OPTIMIZATION NOTES:
// - Structure_Bars: Lower = more swings, Higher = cleaner structure
// - EQ_Tolerance: Adjust based on symbol volatility
// - Min_FVG_ATR: Larger = fewer but higher quality FVGs
// - Premium/Discount: 0.62/0.38 is ICT standard
//
